First, we observe that both optimal and approximation solutions for
the set cover were significantly unfair. This verifies that without
considering fairness, set cover can cause major biases. On the other
hand, formulating the problem as the fair set cover, both the optimal
and the approximation algorithms have zero unfairness. Second,
comparing the average cover size for Opt-SC andOpt-FSC, one can
verify a negligible price of fairness as the avg. cover size increased
by only 0.43 (less than half a set). Last but not least, even though
EffAllPick has a log(𝑛)approximation ratio, in practice, its cover
